{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENtevZAyukmG5G1rBbK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KYoxwRfMaX8ZFT7rQWGpBB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-IgFUak/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: memory writes evicting the static system prompt\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` in `bot.py` put the instructions and the per-athlete context\n(date, profile, zones, goal, facts) into one text block with a single\n`cache_control` marker. The prompt cache is a prefix hash, so every `save_fact`\nchanged the facts inside that block, which invalidated everything after the\nfirst changed byte, including the instructions that never change.\n\n`logs/usage.jsonl` shows this: the call after each `save_fact` has\n`cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and `cache_creation_input_tokens` back at the full\nprompt size.\n\n## Change\n\n`bot.py`, `build_system()`: the system prompt is now two text blocks, each with\n`cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, byte-identical for every athlete and every day.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`, the volatile tail.\n\nA `save_fact` write now invalidates only block two. Nothing else changed: the\ntools array, the message flow and the `save_fact` logic are the same.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun locally without calling the API or touching `data/athletes.json`:\n\n- Block one equals `INSTRUCTIONS` for two different athletes, two dates, and\n  an athlete with added facts.\n- Block two differs once facts change.\n- Both blocks carry a `cache_control` marker.\n- `tools` in the request is unchanged.\n\nI did not send a request to the Anthropic API, so cache hit rates are not yet\nmeasured.\n\n## Open problem: the static block may be below the cache minimum\n\nAnthropic ignores a cache marker when the cacheable prefix up to it is shorter\nthan the model's minimum. For `claude-sonnet-4-5` (the model in `bot.py`) that\nminimum is 1,024 tokens.\n\nThe instructions are about 2,500 characters, roughly 650–800 tokens by my\nestimate. The prefix includes the tools array, which is also above the system\nprompt. The usage log's first call creates about 1,046 cached tokens for tools\nplus system prompt, which implies the static block is around 800–900 tokens.\nSo the marker on block one may be silently ignored, and a memory write would\nstill evict everything, as before. The marker on block two would still cache\nthe full prefix.\n\nI could not confirm the exact token count offline. Two ways to settle it:\n\n- Check the next real call after a `save_fact`: if `cache_creation_input_tokens`\n  is about the size of the tail (~200–250 tokens) and `cache_read_input_tokens`\n  covers the instructions, the fix works. If `cache_creation` is the full prompt\n  again, the static block is still below the minimum.\n- If it is below the minimum, the instructions need to grow by a few hundred\n  tokens of static content to reach 1,024 tokens (or the tools plus\n  instructions together). I did not add padding: the content should be coaching\n  material you choose, not filler. Once the block clears the threshold, the\n  split above does its job.\n\n## Not changed\n\n- Keyword-based tool-group selection sits above the system prompt in the cached\n  prefix, so a message that adds a tool group (e.g. `plan`, `race`) still misses\n  the cache for the whole prompt. This was already the case and the notes call it\n  an acceptable trade-off; I left it alone.\n- Nothing was deployed, committed or reported anywhere outside this directory.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264,"cache_read_input_tokens":39651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a01de13-6568-48fb-a169-7762714394bb","uuid":"01b1dc15-8c83-481d-bbc0-e7d57043a1aa","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:44:46.544Z","request_id":"req_011CgENteevxUmhNCyoQqXXz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KYoxwRfMaX8ZFT7rQWGpBB":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-IgFUak/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: memory writes evicting the static system prompt\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` in `bot.py` put the instructions and the per-athlete context\n(date, profile, zones, goal, facts) into one text block with a single\n`cache_control` marker. The prompt cache is a prefix hash, so every `save_fact`\nchanged the facts inside that block, which invalidated everything after the\nfirst changed byte, including the instructions that never change.\n\n`logs/usage.jsonl` shows this: the call after each `save_fact` has\n`cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and `cache_creation_input_tokens` back at the full\nprompt size.\n\n## Change\n\n`bot.py`, `build_system()`: the system prompt is now two text blocks, each with\n`cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, byte-identical for every athlete and every day.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`, the volatile tail.\n\nA `save_fact` write now invalidates only block two. Nothing else changed: the\ntools array, the message flow and the `save_fact` logic are the same.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun locally without calling the API or touching `data/athletes.json`:\n\n- Block one equals `INSTRUCTIONS` for two different athletes, two dates, and\n  an athlete with added facts.\n- Block two differs once facts change.\n- Both blocks carry a `cache_control` marker.\n- `tools` in the request is unchanged.\n\nI did not send a request to the Anthropic API, so cache hit rates are not yet\nmeasured.\n\n## Open problem: the static block may be below the cache minimum\n\nAnthropic ignores a cache marker when the cacheable prefix up to it is shorter\nthan the model's minimum. For `claude-sonnet-4-5` (the model in `bot.py`) that\nminimum is 1,024 tokens.\n\nThe instructions are about 2,500 characters, roughly 650–800 tokens by my\nestimate. The prefix includes the tools array, which is also above the system\nprompt. The usage log's first call creates about 1,046 cached tokens for tools\nplus system prompt, which implies the static block is around 800–900 tokens.\nSo the marker on block one may be silently ignored, and a memory write would\nstill evict everything, as before. The marker on block two would still cache\nthe full prefix.\n\nI could not confirm the exact token count offline. Two ways to settle it:\n\n- Check the next real call after a `save_fact`: if `cache_creation_input_tokens`\n  is about the size of the tail (~200–250 tokens) and `cache_read_input_tokens`\n  covers the instructions, the fix works. If `cache_creation` is the full prompt\n  again, the static block is still below the minimum.\n- If it is below the minimum, the instructions need to grow by a few hundred\n  tokens of static content to reach 1,024 tokens (or the tools plus\n  instructions together). I did not add padding: the content should be coaching\n  material you choose, not filler. Once the block clears the threshold, the\n  split above does its job.\n\n## Not changed\n\n- Keyword-based tool-group selection sits above the system prompt in the cached\n  prefix, so a message that adds a tool group (e.g. `plan`, `race`) still misses\n  the cache for the whole prompt. This was already the case and the notes call it\n  an acceptable trade-off; I left it alone.\n- Nothing was deployed, committed or reported anywhere outside this directory.\n"}}}
